id: pm-mrvq8u
title: Start-blocker and revision-conflict follow-ups from the PR 1654 CodeRabbit full review
description: "Four Minor CodeRabbit findings from the PR 1654 full review (head 9e5407474), deferred under the bot-loop convergence rule: an incomplete start-path list in docs/CONFIGURATION.md, an unexported ItemRevisionConflictRowFields in the SDK surface snapshot, claim --next ending its walk on a start-blocked candidate, and a post-close dependent revision conflict that tells the caller to retry the already-committed close."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[5]: docs,expected-revision,pm-gh1576,pm-urzubi,start-blockers
created_at: "2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T10:04:18.344Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-03T23:23:25.785Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-03T23:23:25.785Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "The CONFIGURATION.md row names all four start paths (update --status in_progress, claim --start, claim --next --start, start-task); ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported and the regenerated SDK surface snapshot records its fields; claim --next --start skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency and claims the next eligible candidate, with a spec; the post-close dependent_revision_conflict refusal says the close is complete and names only the dependent unblock as the remaining step, with a spec"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "docs/CONFIGURATION.md and docs/COMMANDS.md name all four start paths and the skip; ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported and snapshotted; claimNextFromRecommendations skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency (refused inside the claim's locked mutation, so nothing is written) and reports start_refused on the result, in compact output and in the exhausted refusal's details. The post-close dependent revision conflict says the close is complete and separates two groups: guarded dependents refused for a revision conflict are listed in details.pending_unblock, each with a get step and an unblock step in the caller's tracker scope using the configured open status; dependents whose unblock failed for another reason are listed with their reasons in details.auto_unblock_failed, get only, and must have that cause fixed first. The report is fitted under the error-details ceiling with *_omitted counts, and adds a paged discovery step across every blocked-role status whenever ids or steps were cut."
expected_result: "All four start paths are documented, the row fields type is exported and snapshotted, claim --next --start skips start-blocked candidates, and a post-close dependent conflict names only the unblock as the remaining step"
actual_result: "Verified: start-race.spec.ts drives a real tracker where the blocker lands after ranking and the refused candidate's history is unchanged; claim-command.spec.ts covers the exhausted refusal; item-revision.spec.ts asserts the scoped per-dependent remedy; the suggested unblock command was run in a sandbox (status open, blocked_by edge removed); 100% coverage"
