comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T21:43:04.919Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented all four. (1) docs/CONFIGURATION.md governance.start_blocker_enforcement row names update --status in_progress, claim --start, claim --next --start and start-task, and says claim --next --start skips a refused candidate; docs/COMMANDS.md documents start_refused. (2) ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported from the SDK root; sdk/public-surface.json records it as an additive symbol. (3) claimNextFromRecommendations (src/sdk/lifecycle/claim.ts) skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency (the refusal fires inside the claim's locked mutation, so nothing is written to it), claims the next candidate, and reports skipped ids as start_refused on the available and if-available results and in details.start_refused of the exhausted refusal, whose why now distinguishes start refusals from claims by other agents. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/start-race.spec.ts drives a real tracker where the blocker edge lands after ranking; the refused candidate's history is unchanged. (4) postCloseDependentConflict (src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts) replaces the dependent conflict's required/nextSteps: the close is complete and must not be retried, and the only remaining step is re-reading and unblocking the dependent with pm update <dep> --status open --unset blocked_by --unset blocked_reason --expect-hash <dep>=<item_hash>. That command was verified in a sandbox (status open, blocked_by edge removed). Spec assertions in tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-03T22:55:04.913Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1, fixed: three P2s on the post-close dependent remedy. Recovery commands now carry the caller's tracker scope (--pm-path, --no-extensions) from resolvePmCommandScopeArgs; the unblock uses the configured statusRegistry.open_status instead of a hardcoded open; and the remedy covers every dependent the fan-out left blocked (details.pending_unblock, one get+update step pair per id), not only the first conflict. The conflict is enriched with changes_since before pending_unblock joins its details, so the evidence is kept."
  "2026-11-04T01:17:03.088Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit full review of PR 1658: the post-close remedy now separates guarded dependents refused for a revision conflict (details.pending_unblock, one get+unblock pair each) from dependents whose unblock failed for another reason (details.auto_unblock_failed with each reason, a get step only, and required says to fix that cause first), because repeating the unblock for e.g. a missing history stream under strict policy fails again. Spec: item-revision.spec.ts 'names a dependent whose unblock failed for another reason'. Compact claim --next output now keeps start_refused (core/output/mutation-projection.ts)."
  "2026-11-04T02:24:30.475Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit re-review of PR 1658, fixed: the post-close fan-out report is bounded to 10 ids per list (pending_unblock, auto_unblock_failed with reasons cut to 160 chars) with *_omitted counts and at most 20 next steps, so the details stay under the 4096-byte error-details ceiling instead of being dropped whole; spec with 12 stale dependents. docs/COMMANDS.md now says to confirm every declared blocker is resolved before --unset blocked_by, which removes every blocked_by edge."
  "2026-11-04T03:02:07.290Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 5 (after the CodeRabbit fixes), two P2s fixed: (1) per-list bounds did not bound the merged details object (10 multi-field changes_since entries plus 10 failure reasons reached 4,146 bytes, so the host would drop all details); fitPostCloseDetails now trims auto_unblock_failed, then changes_since, then pending_unblock (keeping one) until isPmCliErrorDetails admits the whole object, counting each dropped entry in its *_omitted field. (2) failure reasons are cut with unicodeSafePrefix so a surrogate pair at offset 159 cannot make the details malformed. Unit specs in close-command.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-04T03:10:27.225Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 6b86e7a98, fixed: when the post-close report omits ids, required and the last next step name a discovery command (pm list --status <configured blocked status> --fields id,title,blocked_by,dependencies --limit 200, in the caller's scope), because the fan-out warnings are dropped with the refusal; nextSteps is capped at 20 combined. COMMANDS.md names the configured open status. Specs assert the details are admitted (<= 4096 bytes) and cover 12 non-conflict failures with long reasons."
  "2026-11-04T03:58:40.312Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 6, fixed: the post-close discovery step lists every status with the blocked role (statusRegistry.blocked_statuses as a CSV --status filter), the same set findAutoUnblockCandidates draws from, not only the default blocked status; a waiting-role dependent past the report limit is no longer stranded."
  "2026-11-04T04:11:06.260Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 33e784761, fixed: the post-close discovery step is also added when the 20-step cap cuts a dependent's step without any id being omitted (9 conflicts + 3 failures = 21 steps), and the required text now says the refusal does not list a step for every dependent left blocked."
  "2026-11-04T05:14:57.933Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 06dd6931e (2 findings), fixed: the exhausted claim --next refusal now speaks of attempted candidates (with --max-attempts 1 a ranked candidate can remain unattempted), and close-command.spec.ts covers the change-evidence trim step of fitPostCloseDetails on its own (30 changes_since entries, no other failures)."
  "2026-11-04T06:30:16.984Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 88641852c (6 Minor), fixed: the exhausted claim --next retry step keeps --start when the request started work (following it can no longer claim without starting) and tells the caller to keep the same filters; the post-close discovery instruction and COMMANDS.md say to continue with --after <next_cursor> while the listing reports has_more."
  "2026-11-04T09:05:33.437Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of b8e03b415, fixed: the post-close required text no longer promises every failure reason when fitPostCloseDetails trimmed some; it says auto_unblock_failed gives the reasons it kept, auto_unblock_failed_omitted counts the rest, and each get step shows the item."
  "2026-11-04T10:04:18.344Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 6181633eb: resolution updated to distinguish revision-conflict dependents (pending_unblock) from other failed unblocks (auto_unblock_failed); COMMANDS.md documents that the discovery step also appears when the 20-step cap cuts steps with both omitted counts zero."
